 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "A single-patient case report of an identifiable person with a stated Blau syndrome diagnosis ('A 32-year-old woman on long-term steroid therapy for Blau syndrome'); NOD2 and any variant are never mentioned, so the variants table is empty.",
 "method_note": "Read by hand; no table transcription. The paper is an ICU case report on mechanical insufflation-exsufflation for post-extubation respiratory failure in COVID-19 ARDS; Blau syndrome is mentioned only as the patient's background diagnosis. No NOD2 gene, variant or genetic testing is mentioned, so no variants row (the paper does not tie a NOD2 variant to the patient). The mother is mentioned only for a positive SARS-CoV-2 PCR test (not tested for NOD2, not described as affected), so she gets no row. No Blau checklist feature is described; all 20 are 'not reported'. Admission vitals (body temperature 36.8 C; blood pressure 150/75 mmHg) were not described as normal or abnormal by the authors and were not used to mark fever or systemic hypertension. The day-13 chest radiograph 'showing no significant abnormal findings' is a normal investigation as a whole and excludes nothing specific. The Discussion describes Blau syndrome as 'a congenital anomaly of the respiratory muscles and skeletal system'; this is a statement about the disease, not a finding in the patient, and was not recorded as a feature. Height 100 cm is recorded in the paper's own words without an HPO candidate (the paper does not say short stature). Vital status 'alive' is inferred from discharge from the ICU. cites_prior_report_of_same_patients is left null (no statement either way). No contradictions found.",
